  "term": "cerebral gigantism",
  "definition": "Cerebral gigantism is an overgrowth syndrome present before or after birth, usually involving unusually large height and head size along with variable delays in motor and cognitive development. It can also occur with other physical and neurological features and is linked to a higher risk of tumors in adulthood.",
